# Trivy accepted-exceptions for the IDP prototype.
# Each entry is a DELIBERATE, reviewed decision — not a blanket mute. New findings
# (any rule not listed here) still fail `trivy config` locally and in CI.
# Revisit these when the prototype hardens beyond Phase 5. See EVALUATION.md backlog.

# GCP-0066 (LOW) — Storage buckets not encrypted with a customer-managed key.
# Accepted: GCS encrypts at rest with Google-managed keys by default, which is
# sufficient for a non-production prototype. CMEK would require standing up a
# KMS key ring + keys + IAM in Phase 0; deferred as future hardening.
GCP-0066

# GCP-0077 (MEDIUM) — Cloud Storage bucket access logging not enabled (state bucket).
# Accepted: access logging needs a separate log-sink bucket. The state bucket is
# already versioned + private (UBLA, public-access-prevention); logging deferred.
# Backlog: enable when we add centralised audit/visibility (Phase 5).
GCP-0077

# GCP-0079 (LOW) — Project-level IAM data-access audit logging not configured.
# Accepted: full audit-log config is out of scope for the prototype's single
# throwaway project; admin-activity logs are on by default. Deferred.
GCP-0079

# GCP-0010 (HIGH) — Default network created at project level.
# Accepted (config-level) for now: the fix (auto_create_network = false) is a
# CREATE-time-only property, so it cannot be flipped on the already-provisioned
# project — real remediation is deleting the existing default network out of band.
# Tracked as a backlog item in EVALUATION.md; no compute/ingress uses it today.
GCP-0010
